      "writtenOn": "2023-07-19T15:04:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do you mean aosp/2626248?\n\nYes\n\n\u003e Could you give a link to what you think would be better as a data property?\n\n[rust_library](https://github.com/bazelbuild/rules_rust/blob/main/docs/defs.md#rust_library) rule has 4 attributes to supply rust files\n1. `crate_root`: the entry file passed to `rustc` for building a crate.\n2. `srcs`: list of rust files used to build the library. `crate_root` can be left unset of one of the `srcs` has a file named `lib.rs`\n3. `compile_data`: list of rust files used at compile time\n4. `data`: list of rust files used at compile time and [runtime](https://github.com/daivinhtran/rules_rust/blob/main/rust/private/rustc.bzl#L1367-L1369).\n\nYou are right that the other files are (and were) currently ingested by rustc. That means `Toolchain_compile_data` or just `Compile_data` is a better name for the sake of making it easier to convert 1-to-1 props in Soong and attributes to Bazel.\n\nSince now that we have a chance to do it better, I think it\u0027s good to err on the side of Bazel\u0027s convention to ease the conversion.",
